{
  "_comment": "Interview knowledge the DV-105(A) field config cannot express. DV-105(A) comes in when DV-105 item 4a is answered No (\"If no, complete form DV-105(A). Do not complete the section below.\"), so everything here is asked only then, and DV-105 item 4 is not. Each group is one child, or children who have always lived together: its names, then its homes from the current one back, as DV-105 item 4 asks them - one address at a time behind \"Did these children live somewhere else ...?\", up to the seven rows the paper prints. There are always two groups, because the children did not all live together. The box under item 3 asks for a third: answered Yes, it ticks and the second copy of DV-105(A) comes in.",
